From 188353939d61ecd61e8d008922846c900bfb5ad6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 07:56:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 180/274] Sink rejection on by default for DeepSeek V4.1, its
 column and threshold in one table

The attention-sink collapse (a sampled token's residual running away in one
channel, its next-token distribution turning into document-start noise) is
DeepSeek V4.1 Flash checkpoint behaviour: DeepSeek's reference reproduces it
on the 1017 checkpoint. The detector and draft-zero rejection were off unless
VLLM_SINK_DETECTOR_COLUMN and VLLM_SINK_REJECTION were set. They now default
on for the architectures listed in vllm.v1.sample.sink.SINK_CHANNELS, which
holds each one's watched column and threshold (DeepseekV41ForCausalLM: 2455,
85,000), and stay off for every other model. VLLM_SINK_REJECTION stays the
switch: 0 turns detector and rejection off. The column and threshold
settings become overrides with no defaults of their own; with rejection off,
an explicit column still runs the detector alone (lab surveys).

The switch and the one table mark the code that exists only for these
checkpoints: a model without the behaviour drops its entry, and a later one
can remove the sink modules (vllm/v1/sample/sink.py,
vllm/v1/worker/gpu/sample/sink.py) and the scheduler's draft-zero hook.

SinkConfig.for_model(vllm_config) replaces from_env() at its three call sites
(scheduler, V2 runner, the SM120 model's column capture). The V1 runner has no
detector, so the worker refuses to start it while the detector is on, rather
than letting the scheduler hold tokens for a verification nothing does.
VLLM_SINK_REJECTION leaves the compile-key exclusions: it now decides whether
the forward keeps the column.

Base: local-inference-lab integration/karmic-kraken-beta 19f2c20e + the r6x
series (7316c7f9f) + 0185, 0221 (sink rejection v2, gated on the TP3
triangle 2026-10-20) and 0222 (late admission).

Quality: on DeepSeek V4.1 the defaults equal the gated settings (column
2455, threshold 85,000, rejection on, three alternates). No other model
changes.

Tests: tests/v1/core/test_sink_draft_zero.py (on by default for
DeepseekV41ForCausalLM; switched off; off for other models and refused when
forced on without a column; an explicit column runs the detector alone and
replaces the model's; the scheduler suites name their test model's column
and build it from a local OPT config, so they run offline without a
tokenizer, as the release tests do).

Upstream status: local; not proposed.

